//
// Conduit (--use-conduit) end-to-end run for the canon
// refuse-to-collapse-on-await predicate (`chainHasAwait` in
// CanonicalizeChannelPutsUtils.{h,cpp}, landed 2026-05-03 in this
// commit) — the gets-side variant.  Companion to:
//   test/Dialect/Conduit/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_token_true.mlir
//     (lit-only at-site pin for the predicate)
//   test/npu-xrt/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_link/conduit.lit
//     (link-refusal HW smoke; structural sibling, different predicate)
//   test/npu-xrt/conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_puts_with_await/conduit.lit
//     (puts-side counterpart of THIS smoke)
//
// Validates that canon's ArithProgressionPattern (and
// HomogeneousRepeatPattern, symmetric) does NOT collapse 4 sliding-
// offset gets on a NON-LINKED compute-S2MM → shim channel when each
// get carries `aiex.dma_await_task` (per-issue ack) +
// `aiex.dma_free_task` (release marker) — chain shape `[true, false]`
// after dma-task-to-conduit lowering.  The fixture also pins the
// LEGITIMATE collapse path on the puts side (chain `[false]` only on
// 4 identical free-only puts on @in collapse to 1 + dma_repeat = 3)
// so the predicate doesn't over-refuse.
//
// Pre-fix on the gets side, collapse → 1 configure × outer wrap dim
// <size = 4, stride = 64> with the per-issue ack request inherited
// onto the merged single configure → firmware fires the BD 4 times
// back-to-back without per-chunk producer-side ack pacing → HW stalls
// (XRT timeout).  Same root-cause class as the canon link-refusal
// landed in commit 375b0e5233.
//
// Post-fix, canon refuses on `chainHasAwait(refShape)` for the gets;
// Pass C emits 4 separate paced shim configures (each with its own
// per-issue ack); HW dispatch completes and the per-byte output check
// below passes.
//
// Pipeline: bare `--use-conduit` (no fusion flags — this test exercises
// canon refusal, not fusion).  aiecc.cpp:1492-1508 expands `--use-conduit`
// to `objectfifo-to-conduit, dma-task-to-conduit, conduit-canonicalize-
// channel-puts, conduit-depth-promote, conduit-to-dma`.
//
// PASS expectation: dispatch completes and output bytes match the
// spec-derived reference computed in test.cpp.  Hang/timeout would
// indicate the canon refusal regressed; wrong-bytes would indicate
// the chainHasAwait emit shape changed in a non-byte-equivalent way
// (or the puts-side LEGITIMATE collapse silently broke).
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai, peano
//
// Kernel compute is inline bf16 load/store (the in-core scf.for copy
// loop in aie.mlir); Peano is required because xchesscc cannot select
// bf16 ops for an inline core (sibling pattern: `loadpdi/run.lit`,
// `vec_vec_add_objfifo_init/aie2.py`, `conduit_join_last_slice_overflow/
// conduit.lit`, `conduit_canon_no_collapse_on_link/conduit.lit`).  Use
// `--no-xchesscc --no-xbridge` to route the kernel compile through Peano.
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu1_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --no-xchesscc --no-xbridge --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
